cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "VECTRI-ABM"
abstract: >-
  An agent-based model of disease transmission coupled to the VECTRI
  vector-ecology model (Tompkins et al. 2013). The framework resolves individual human agents on a
  climate-driven grid, with age-structured diagnostics including
  per-timestep symptomatic and asymptomatic incidence & age-dependent acquisition and
  waning of immunity. Calibration tools - Sobol sensitivity analysis (SALiB), a genetic
  algorithm (Tompkins et al. 2018) and an integration to the Optuna calibration suite are included. Agent
  mobility is defined but not yet functional. The underlying agent-based framework is
  named MoBILE (Mobility-Based Integrated Landscape Epidemiology), which remains the
  repository name; VECTRI-ABM is the disease model built on it.
type: software
